      <section class="page-hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
        <div class="page-hero-inner">
          <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
          <h1 id="page-title">The site should work for everyone who visits it.</h1>
          <p class="page-lead">Effective date: September 9, 2025</p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="content-section narrow" aria-labelledby="target-title">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2 id="target-title">The target</h2>
          <p>
            Tectori's target for this website is Web Content Accessibility
            Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 level AA. The site is reviewed against that
            target as content changes.
          </p>
          <h2>What the site does today</h2>
          <p>
            Pages use semantic HTML with landmarks, headings, and labeled
            navigation. Every page starts with a skip to content link.
            Images carry text alternatives. Form fields on the login preview
            have visible labels. Navigation, including the mobile menu, works
            with a keyboard. Text and background colors are chosen for
            contrast and readability.
          </p>
          <h2>Known limits</h2>
          <p>
            The site is reviewed with automated checks and manual testing
            rather than a formal external audit. Some issues may not be
            caught before a visitor finds them.
          </p>
          <h2>Report an issue</h2>
          <p>
            If any part of this site is hard to use with assistive
            technology, use the contact page or call <span class="nowrap">(615) 829-6802</span>
            to tell Tectori directly. Reports go straight to the founder and
            are treated as defects, not feedback for a backlog.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
